      "name": null,
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{4p-1}{2(2p+2)}$ for $p=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $p$ with $4$ in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4p-1}{2(2p+2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(4)-1}{2(2(4)+2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{2(8+2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{15}{20} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
