      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{p+9}{2(3-p)}$ for $p=-5.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $p$ with $-5$ in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{p+9}{2(3-p)} & = \\\\ \\frac{(-5)+9}{2(3-(-5))} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{2(8)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{16} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
